{
 "version": 2,
 "_about": "The fantasy painting world Aurelind: ONE seamless map (rules: core/fantasy_terrain.gd, drawn by game/fantasy_world.gd). Positions are metres from the world centre, x east, z south. ROUND 5: every distance between places is three times what it was (size 6000; places keep their own size; a lake, the spawn and the way out keep their offset to the place they belong to); there is NO fast travel (director). Regions blend into each other; nothing blocks the way, only the level of what lives there. height: base = ground level, amp = hill height, rough = hill size (bigger = wider hills), then the region's LANDFORMS (core/fantasy_terrain.gd `_landforms`; all fade out at places, along paths and round lakes): ridge {amp, rough, sharp} = mountain ridges; mesa {height, rough, level (higher = less table land), edge (smaller = steeper cliff)} = table land, with a small rough stone pillars; gorge {depth, rough, width} = winding cuts; dunes {amp, length} = waves of sand; terrace {step, soft} = the slope in steps; cone {place, open_to, crater, rim, radius, height} = a volcano round that place with its way in facing the other. After changing any of it raise RULES_VERSION in core/fantasy_terrain.gd (saved charts). ground: [low colour, high colour, cliff colour]. mood: fog colour and density, sky top and horizon, ambient and sun colour. trees: {model: how many per chunk}. clutter: {model: how many per chunk} = solid boulders, rock spires, logs, stumps and bushes scattered through the open country (models tools/blender/fantasy_clutter.py; at most 12 a chunk). nodes: {node id: how many per chunk}. Placeholders for the director. tuft: grass or wheat blades scattered over the ground (base colour, tip colour, how many per chunk, height). scheme: which colour set of cottages and halls a region's towns use. npcs.look: body, outfit and hair (ids from data/appearance.json and data/outfits.json). surface: the ground texture of a region (data/surfaces.json g_*). fish: which fishing node a region's fresh water and its sea shore give. places.yard: the trodden ground of a place. lakes: ponds and lakes cut into the land (water: fresh | lava). roads: pairs of places joined by a path. ALL NAMES AND SPOKEN LINES are in data/fantasy/writing/*.txt (core/fantasy_data.gd puts them back in when the game loads).",
